.\" conflux(5): the config file. config.example.toml documents every option at
.\" its default and docs/FEATURES.md has longer examples; keep the three in step.
.TH CONFLUX 5 "" "conflux" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
conflux \- configuration of the conflux sync daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I \(ti/.config/conflux/config.toml
.br
.I /etc/conflux/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR conflux (1)
reads one TOML file:
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/conflux/config.toml
in the user scope,
.I \(ti/.config/conflux/config.toml
unless
.B \%XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set;
.TP
.I /etc/conflux/config.toml
in the system scope.
.PP
.B \-\-config
or
.B CONFLUX_CONFIG
name another.
.PP
The file has an optional
.B [daemon]
table with daemon-wide settings and the defaults every sync inherits, any number
of
.B [[remote]]
tables, each a place to sync with, and one
.B [[sync]]
table per sync group: a local directory and the rules for keeping it in step.
.PP
A sync group does one of two jobs.
Either it syncs files against a remote, comparing the two trees and copying
single files, which is what most options are about; or it sets
.B git_repo
to keep a git clone up to date through git itself (see
.BR "GIT CLONES" ).
.PP
The daemon refuses a file with errors, and
.B conflux config validate
checks one as the daemon would.
The app, Conflux, edits the same file in place, keeping its comments and
layout.
.SH VALUES
.TP
.I duration
A string such as
.BR \(dq500ms\(dq ,
.BR \(dq2s\(dq ,
.BR \(dq3m\(dq ,
.BR \(dq1h\(dq ;
.B \(dq0s\(dq
turns the setting off.
.TP
.I size
A number of bytes, or a string with a unit:
.BR KB ,
.BR MB ,
.BR GB ,
.B TB
(powers of 1000) or
.BR KiB ,
.BR MiB ,
.B GiB
(powers of 1024), such as
.BR \(dq100MB\(dq .
.B 0
means no limit.
.TP
.I path
A leading
.B \(ti
and
.BI $ VARIABLES
are expanded.
In the system scope
.B \(ti
is the home of the
.B conflux
user, so write paths there in full.
.TP
.I glob
Relative to the group's local directory.
.B *
matches within one path segment,
.B **
across segments, and a plain name matches its whole subtree.
.TP
.I command
Run with
.BR "sh \-c" ,
in the daemon's environment; its standard output is the value, without the
trailing newline.
.SH [daemon]
.TP
.B log_level
What the daemon logs:
.BR error ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
.B debug
or
.BR trace .
.B CONFLUX_LOG
overrides it.
Default
.BR info .
.TP
.B profile
The profile the daemon runs, unless
.B \-\-profile
names one.
Default
.BR default .
.PP
The rest are defaults, which a sync's own setting overrides; for
.B pull_interval
and
.B max_file_size
a remote's setting comes in between.
.TP
.B debounce
.RI ( duration )
How long a
.B watch
trigger waits for changes to settle before syncing.
Default
.BR 5s .
.TP
.B interval
.RI ( duration )
How often a
.B timer
trigger syncs.
Default
.BR 1h .
.TP
.B pull_interval
.RI ( duration )
How often to run an extra pull-only sync, which brings in changes made on the
remote side, whatever the trigger.
Default: every
.B 5m
for anything git (a
.B git
remote or a
.B git_repo
clone), as neither can be watched; off for the rest.
.TP
.B empty_dirs
.B ignore
leaves empty directories alone,
.B prune
removes them from both sides after a sync,
.B mirror
creates and removes them on both sides.
Has no effect with git, which cannot store them.
Default
.BR ignore .
.TP
.B deletions
.B deny
never deletes a file on either side, whatever the scope: a file removed on one
side stays on the other.
.B allow
removes it on the other side too.
Default
.BR deny .
.TP
.B max_file_size
.RI ( size )
Larger files are skipped, in both directions.
Default
.BR 100MB .
.TP
.B exclude
.RI ( globs )
Never synced, in any group: added to each group's own
.BR exclude .
By default the clutter of version control and file managers, anywhere in the
tree:
.RS
.IP
.EX
["**/.git/**", "**/.svn/**", "**/.hg/**",
 "**/.DS_Store", "**/Thumbs.db", "**/*.swp"]
.EE
.RE
.IP
.B []
syncs them all.
Conflict copies are always excluded.
.SH [[remote]]
.TP
.B id
Its name, which a sync's
.B remote
refers to.
Required.
.TP
.B backend
.BR webdav ,
.B git
or
.BR filesystem .
Required.
.TP
.B url
Where it is: a WebDAV base URL, a git repository URL
.RB ( https:// ,
.B ssh://
or
.IB user @ host : path\fR),
or for
.B filesystem
a directory
.RI ( path ).
Required.
.TP
.B label
A description, shown by the app.
.TP
.BR username ", " password ", " password_command
Credentials for WebDAV and for git over HTTPS.
.B password_command
.RI ( command )
keeps the password out of the file, such as
.BR "secret\-tool lookup service conflux" .
.TP
.B identity_file
.RI ( path )
The private key for git over SSH.
.TP
.B identity_file_command
.RI ( command )
Prints the private key for git over SSH, so it needs no file.
.TP
.B branch
The git branch to sync with.
Default: the repository's default branch.
.TP
.B commit_msg_command
.RI ( command )
Prints the message of the commits made to a git remote; it runs in conflux's
clone, so it can look at what is staged.
Default:
.BI "conflux sync from " hostname\fR.
.TP
.BR pull_interval ", " max_file_size
Override the
.B [daemon]
defaults for this remote's groups.
.SH [[sync]]
.SS Identity
.TP
.B id
A name for the group, which
.B conflux sync
takes; unique among the syncs.
.TP
.B label
A description, shown by the app.
.SS Mapping
Set exactly one of
.BR remote ,
.B remote_fs
and
.BR git_repo .
.TP
.B remote
The
.B id
of a
.BR [[remote]] .
.TP
.B remote_fs
.RI ( path )
A directory to sync with, for which conflux makes the
.B filesystem
remote itself: no
.B [[remote]]
needed.
.TP
.B git_repo
.RI ( path )
A git clone to keep up to date through git, which is also the group's local
directory (see
.BR "GIT CLONES" ).
.TP
.B local
.RI ( path )
The local directory.
Required, unless
.B git_repo
gives it.
.TP
.B remote_path
The directory of the remote that
.B local
corresponds to.
Default: the remote's root.
.SS What is synced
.TP
.B include
.RI ( globs )
What the group syncs, both ways.
Default
.BR [] ,
which matches nothing;
.B [\(dq**\(dq]
matches everything.
.TP
.B scope
What happens to the paths outside
.BR include :
.RS
.TP
.B include
Nothing: they are never pushed, pulled or deleted.
So a remote pointed at the home directory cannot touch files not listed.
The default.
.TP
.B remote
Pulled down from the remote, which wins over local changes (a local copy that
differed is kept as a conflict copy).
Good for dotfiles.
.TP
.B local
Pushed up, the local copy winning.
.TP
.B mirror
The whole tree syncs both ways, and
.B include
is ignored.
With
.B deletions
allowed, a deletion on one side, or an empty remote, can remove every file on
the other: use it only for a directory meant to be a mirror.
.RE
.TP
.B exclude
.RI ( globs )
Never synced, in addition to the
.B [daemon]
list.
.TP
.B deletions
As in
.BR [daemon] .
.TP
.BR empty_dirs ", " max_file_size
As in
.BR [daemon] .
.SS When it syncs
.TP
.B trigger
.B watch
syncs on local changes, after
.BR debounce ;
.B watch\-both
also watches the remote, which must be a directory
.RB ( filesystem
or
.BR remote_fs );
.B timer
syncs every
.BR interval ;
.B manual
only on
.BR "conflux sync" .
Default
.BR watch .
Whatever the trigger, the daemon syncs every group once when it starts.
.TP
.BR debounce ", " interval ", " pull_interval
As in
.BR [daemon] .
.SS Other
.TP
.B profiles
The profiles whose daemons run this group.
Without it the group is in the
.B default
profile only; a list is taken as written, so
.B []
puts the group in none.
.TP
.B commit_msg_command
.RI ( command )
For a
.B git_repo
group: prints the message of its commits.
Default:
.BI "conflux sync from " hostname\fR.
.SH CONFLICTS
When a file changed on both sides since the last sync, the newer one stays in
place and the other is kept next to it as a conflict copy, named like
.PP
.RS
.EX
report.conflux\-conflict\-2026\-10\-31_14\-05\-09.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Conflict copies are never synced.
A git remote stores no time per file, so its files count as changed when the
branch was last committed to.
.SH GIT CLONES
A
.B git_repo
group keeps a clone that already exists up to date with git: on every sync it
commits the changes in the working tree, fetches, fast-forwards or rebases its
own commits onto the upstream branch, and pushes.
The branch, its upstream and the credentials are the clone's own,
.I .gitignore
decides what is tracked, and the commits are authored with the clone's
.B user.name
and
.BR user.email .
.PP
Work in progress is committed, starting with the sync at the daemon's startup.
When the rebase conflicts it is aborted and reported: the local commits stay,
nothing is pushed, and
.B git pull \-\-rebase
resolves it by hand.
History is otherwise never rewritten.
A clone that is missing, has a detached HEAD or a branch without upstream, or is
in the middle of a merge or rebase is refused until fixed.
.PP
Only
.BR id ,
.BR label ,
.BR trigger
(but not
.BR watch\-both ),
.BR interval ,
.BR debounce ,
.BR pull_interval ,
.B commit_msg_command
and
.B profiles
apply; the file-level options
.RB ( remote_path ,
.BR include ,
.BR scope ,
.BR deletions ,
.BR empty_dirs ,
.BR max_file_size )
are refused.
.SH GIT AUTHENTICATION
A
.B git_repo
clone authenticates as
.BR git (1)
would.
A
.B git
remote over SSH tries, in order,
.B identity_file
or
.BR identity_file_command ,
the
.B IdentityFile
entries for the host in
.IR \(ti/.ssh/config ,
.BR ssh\-agent (1),
then the default keys
.RI ( \(ti/.ssh/id_ed25519 ,
.IR id_ecdsa ,
.IR id_rsa ).
Other
.BR ssh_config (5)
settings, such as
.BR ProxyJump ,
.B Hostname
or
.BR Include ,
are not used.
Over HTTPS it uses
.B username
and
.B password
or
.BR password_command .
.SH EXAMPLES
Dotfiles from a git repository: everything in it is pulled into the home
directory, and only the listed paths are pushed back.
.PP
.RS
.EX
[[remote]]
id = "dotfiles"
backend = "git"
url = "git@github.com:me/dotfiles.git"

[[sync]]
remote = "dotfiles"
local = "\(ti"
scope = "remote"
include = [".bashrc", ".config/nvim"]
trigger = "timer"
interval = "15m"
.EE
.RE
.PP
A folder kept the same as one on a Nextcloud server:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[[remote]]
id = "nextcloud"
backend = "webdav"
url = "https://cloud.example.com/remote.php/dav/files/me/"
username = "me"
password_command = "secret\-tool lookup service conflux"

[[sync]]
remote = "nextcloud"
local = "\(ti/Documents"
remote_path = "documents"
scope = "mirror"
deletions = "allow"
.EE
.RE
.PP
A backup disk, synced on changes on either side, in the
.B laptop
profile only:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[[sync]]
remote_fs = "/mnt/backup/documents"
local = "\(ti/Documents"
scope = "mirror"
trigger = "watch\-both"
profiles = ["laptop"]
.EE
.RE
.PP
A notes repository already cloned:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[[sync]]
git_repo = "\(ti/notes"
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/conflux/config.example.toml
Every option, commented out at its default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conflux (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
.PP
More examples:
.br
.UR https://github.com/AperteDev/conflux/blob/master/docs/FEATURES.md
.UE
